        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 92b03138bac022b1f2b4e7d9befc64bcbf4a341a2c69f573cb2d172e209eb668\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: be7b76e01ac1552507d597bc518d3f8e7b15b5dd161c599fed26853b3dad2bcf\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the router to filter PIM register messages received from a multicast DR for any undesirable multicast groups and sources. The example below will deny any multicast streams for groups 239.5.0.0/16 and allow from only sources 10.1.2.6 and 10.1.2.7. \n\nR2(config)#ip access-list extended PIM_REGISTER_FILTER\nR2(config-ext-nacl)#deny ip any 239.5.0.0 0.0.255.255\nR2(config-ext-nacl)#permit ip host 10.1.2.6 any\nR2(config-ext-nacl)#permit ip host 10.1.2.7 any\nR2(config-ext-nacl)#deny ip any any\nR2(config-ext-nacl)#exit\nR2(config)#ip pim accept-register list PIM_REGISTER_FILTER\nR2(config)#end",
