          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 92b03138bac022b1f2b4e7d9befc64bcbf4a341a2c69f573cb2d172e209eb668\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: be7b76e01ac1552507d597bc518d3f8e7b15b5dd161c599fed26853b3dad2bcf\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the router to drop IPv6 packets containing an option type value of 0x8A (Endpoint Identification) regardless of whether it appears in a Hop-by-Hop or Destination Option header as shown in the example below.\n\nR1(config)#ipv6 access-list FILTER_IPV6\nR1(config-ipv6-acl)#deny 60 any any dest-option log\nR1(config-ipv6-acl)#deny hbh any any dest-option log\nR1(config-ipv6-acl)#permit …\n…\n…\n…\nR1(config-ipv6-acl)#deny ipv6 any any log\nR1(config-ipv6-acl)#exit\nR1(config)#int g1/0\nR1(config-if)#ipv6 traffic-filter FILTER_IPV6\nR1(config-if)#end",
